      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter amlodipine 50 mg once daily, even with your confirmation. There's no recognized use of amlodipine at that dose. It's five times the maximum daily dose, and at that level the risk of serious harm is real: severe, prolonged low blood pressure, shock, and fluid in the lungs that isn't caused by the heart. It also wouldn't help more: 10 mg is the ceiling because higher doses add little blood-pressure benefit and more side effects. An order that looks like an extra zero is exactly what this check is meant to catch, so confirming the same number doesn't settle it.\n\nHere's what I can do now:\n- **Enter amlodipine 5 mg by mouth, once daily** (likely what was meant), or\n- **Enter amlodipine 10 mg by mouth, once daily** if you want the maximum dose, or\n- **Enter another dose between 2.5 and 10 mg.**\n\nIf you have a specific clinical reason for a dose above 10 mg, please go through pharmacy or the attending. They can review and verify it, and the order can be entered through your hospital's override process with that sign-off documented.\n\nJust tell me which dose to enter and I'll do it right away."
      }
